#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# apart_square_free

#% text
# `apart_square_free(e, x)` writes the rational function e of x as a polynomial plus terms `a/d^j`, d running over the square-free factors of its denominator and deg a < deg d.

#% text
# `apart_square_free(e)` does this in the last variable of e.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The denominator is not factored beyond its square-free factors (and the factors it is written with), unlike `apart`.

#% item
# Lists, equations, inequalities and logical combinations are handled element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
apart_square_free((x^2 - 2)/(x^4 - 2*x^2 + 1))
#% output
#= -1/(-1 + x^2)^2 + (-1 + x^2)^-1

#% cell
apart((x^2 - 2)/(x^4 - 2*x^2 + 1))
#% output
#= -3/(4*(1 + x)) - 1/(4*(-1 + x)^2) - 1/(4*(1 + x)^2) + 3/(4*(-1 + x))

#% cell
apart_square_free(24*((x^2 - 1)/((x^4 - 2*x^2 + 1)*(x + 5))))
#% output
#= (5 - x)/(-1 + x^2) + (5 + x)^-1

#% cell
apart_square_free((x^2 + x*y + y^2)/(x^4 - 2*x^2*y^2 + y^4), x)
#% output
#= (2*y^2 + x*y)/(-y^2 + x^2)^2 + (-y^2 + x^2)^-1

#% cell
apart_square_free((x - 1)/(x*(x + 1)^2))
#% output
#= -1/x + 2/(1 + x)^2 + (1 + x)^-1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `apart`, `partial_fractions`, `together`, `factor_square_free_list`
